From 5895dbe7d4c9d86880b6cc6e4ffc66e29915e129 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@aosp-vm>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:04:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] netbpfload: do not reboot when the BPF loader fails (debug /
 tolerate old-kernel BPF limits on the Duo)

On the Surface Duo 2 (5.4 kernel, R-era vendor) android-16.0.0_r4 reboots about 25 seconds into every boot:
NetBpfLoad logs "DO NOT EXPECT SYSTEM TO BOOT SUCCESSFULLY", sleeps 20 s, returns 38, and init reboots
(reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed). Letting the boot continue exposes the real error in logcat.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I21fe60d234a48269ef044710388705d7853eb9ef
---
 bpf/loader/netbpfload.35rc | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bpf/loader/netbpfload.35rc b/bpf/loader/netbpfload.35rc
index a23bd60e10..51e7f0bf9a 100644
--- a/bpf/loader/netbpfload.35rc
+++ b/bpf/loader/netbpfload.35rc
@@ -65,5 +65,8 @@ service bpfloader /apex/com.android.tethering/bin/netbpfload
     #    'cannot prove return value is 0 or 1' or 'unsupported / unknown operation / helper',
     #    'invalid bpf_context access', etc.
     #
-    reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
+    # Duo: do not reboot when the BPF loader fails, so the device boots and the reason can be read
+    # with: adb logcat -s 'bpfloader:*' 'LibBpfLoader:*' 'NetBpfLoad:*' 'NetBpfLoader:*'
+    # (AOSP's own debugging recipe for 'bpfloader-failed' bootloops, see the comment above)
+    # reboot_on_failure reboot,bpfloader-failed
     override
-- 
2.43.0

